# Northwind commerce

Northwind is an opt-in NetScript showcase. It uses the same Utility pages,
typed services and background plugins as an ordinary generated application.
The sample contains 40 orders, five customers, eight products and 80 line items.
Money is stored in integer minor units; totals come from the saved line items.

## Start the showcase

Install Deno 2.9.7, the pinned Aspire CLI and Docker, then run:

```sh
netscript init northwind --from showcase --ci --yes
cd northwind
deno task showcase:setup
deno task aspire:start
```

The setup task installs streams, workers, sagas and triggers using the supported
plugin commands, copies the app-owned commerce resources, generates registries,
and initializes, generates and seeds the database. No manual linking or source
edits are required. SQLite is the default; `--db postgres` selects PostgreSQL.
The first PostgreSQL database lifecycle is provisioned through Aspire by the CLI.
Existing related orders are preserved on reseed.

Open the web app URL shown by Aspire. Overview shows saved orders, revenue,
status charts and activity. Orders supports search, status filters, sorting and
CSV export. Customers and Products read the same live database through oRPC.

## Follow an order

1. Open Orders, then an order that is pending, awaiting payment or paid.
2. Select **Fulfil order**. Refresh the order to see durable worker progress.
3. The order saga records **Order**, **Payment** and **Shipping** steps. Its
   payment is a demonstration transition, with no external charge.
4. Return to Overview. The stream activity includes the committed status changes.
5. The order detail also provides **Send delivery webhook**, which uses the
   registered webhook trigger to enqueue the same fulfilment job.

The webhook is deliberately public sample ingress for local development. Replace
its the sample `memory` verifier with your verifier before exposing it outside your demo.
Sign in shows the normal authentication connection surface. Connect an identity
provider through the supported auth plugin command when you need protected access.
The Assistant page explains provider connection when no model is configured.

## Extend the application

Start here. `contracts/commerce.contract.ts` owns customer/product/line schemas;
`services/orders/src/commerce.ts` implements live reads. The standard orders
contract and repository remain under `contracts/versions/v1/` and
`services/orders/src/`. `database/{{dbEngine}}/scripts/seed-commerce.ts` owns the
catalogue; the ordinary sample seed owns the dated order backbone.

`workers/jobs/fulfil-order.ts`, `sagas/order-fulfilment/order-saga.ts` and
`triggers/order-webhook.ts` are the background extension points. The shared
Utility views remain under `apps/{{appName}}/routes/(_components)/`; the additive
order workflow view is `order-workflow.tsx`. All plugin runtime code belongs to
the installed packages. `showcase/resources/` retains the original recipe sources.
